    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0272" n="1106" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112Sa/80a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-27T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1918—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3007. For Dresel [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 120. Sailing vessels carrying “safe-conducts” from the German Government will
                    for the time being be permitted to sail from United States ports to Cette with
                    cargoes destined to Switzerland, provided such cargoes are not
                        objectionable.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d237-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d237-f1" n="2" xml:id="d237-f1-content">
                <p>See also telegram to the Ambassador in Great Britain, No. 1648, Sept. 27, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg997">p. 997</ref>.</p>
            </note>
